  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nSurface high pressure and northerly flow aloft will continue to keep \nthe area dry and cool for the remainder of today. Areas of fog will \nbe possible again tonight, particularly in sheltered valleys, along \nwith patchy frost expected in spots, mainly across parts of the \nmountains in sheltered valleys. \n\nThe area should remain dry, cool, and mostly sunny through the \nweekend, although a few clouds may appear from time to time \nparticularly across the east as low pressure slowly rides north \nalong the coast. In addition, a few light showers are possible \nacross the far northeast on Sunday afternoon/evening as moisture \nspreads east of this low. Gradually warmer conditions take hold to \nstart next week as ridging builds in ahead of the next approaching \nsystem, progged to affect the area by mid to late week.",
